  m_Name: Job_Pergola
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: WoodcraftSimulator::WoodcraftSimulator.Jobs.JobDefinition
  id: pergola-job
  displayName: Garden pergola
  description: "A free-standing pergola 3 \xD7 3 m beside the terrace: pier blocks,
    four plumb posts, two beams, five rafters."
  blueprint: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3192a9caa043a8942b1a9c48663a5e56, type: 2}
  stockSpecies: {fileID: 11400000, guid: dca24a1dc39899146a557f009cce814a, type: 2}
  stockLengthMillimeters: 3000
  stockWidthMillimeters: 120
  stockThicknessMillimeters: 45
  spareBoards: 0
  tips:
  - Outside, right of the terrace. Set out the site at the corner stake, then dig
    and gravel the four pier spots.
  - 'Cut the posts to 2200 mm on the sawhorses. A post never goes in exactly vertical:
    hold the spirit level against two neighbouring faces, push it upright with the
    wheel, then nail a temporary brace (left mouse button).'
  - 'Only braced posts can be fastened or carry a beam. Beams and rafters are higher
    than you can reach: carry the stepladder there, climb it with Space.'
  - The customer paid half as a deposit for the material; the rest comes on delivery.
  payEuros: 850
  requiresFinish: 0
